{"duration": 59.025, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "A Russian engineer hammers copper plates onto a ship\u2019s hull, sparks flying.", "start": 0.08, "end": 3.899}, {"beat": 0, "text": "He aims to stop the invisible enemies that cling beneath the waves.", "start": 4.119, "end": 7.605}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Fellow shipwrights laugh, warning the metal will rust and sink their fleet.", "start": 8.025, "end": 11.452}, {"beat": 1, "text": "They claim the extra weight will slow every vessel to a crawl.", "start": 11.672, "end": 14.746}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Lomonosov orders the copper nailed beneath the waterline in St.\u202fPetersburg.", "start": 15.166, "end": 19.87}, {"beat": 2, "text": "The ship leaves the dock still covered in thick, green slime.", "start": 20.09, "end": 23.064}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Barnacles and shipworm have already turned the hull into a barn.", "start": 23.284, "end": 26.488}, {"beat": 3, "text": "You see how a greasy pan sticks to food \u2013 the slime drags a ship the same way.", "start": 26.908, "end": 30.601}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Copper reacts with seawater, forming a thin copper\u2011oxy\u2011chloride film that is poisonous to marine life.", "start": 31.021, "end": 36.845}, {"beat": 4, "text": "The film dissolves constantly, so barnacles and shipworm cannot attach.", "start": 37.065, "end": 41.048}, {"beat": 4, "text": "With the slime gone, the hull slices through water, gaining precious speed.", "start": 41.268, "end": 45.003}, {"beat": 5, "text": "The navy dubs the vessel \u2018copper\u2011bottomed,\u2019 a mark of quality that cuts insurance premiums.", "start": 45.423, "end": 50.422}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Ironically, the same copper that saved speed later sparked a bolt\u2011corrosion crisis, forcing engineers to redesign fasteners.", "start": 50.642, "end": 57.905}], "words": [{"w": "A", "start": 0.145, "end": 0.195, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "Russian", "start": 0.245, "end": 0.52, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, 